From 99a2f73095fab7db577b92045cab9cddcc26019d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:09:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tui obligation: an update pause's killed job is
 reported once from the marker

Follow-up of PR #2159's review nits (review 5891172793, card t_01a1d4f4d37f1469).

1. Managed-worker owner:"tui" intent (documented + pinned). A single-profile managed worker
   inherits the Desktop backend's env byte-for-byte (`_worker_env` returns None), so
   `is_desktop_owned_backend()` is True inside it and a Desktop chat's notify job finishing there
   stamps an owner:"tui" delivery_obligation with the worker's pid. That is intended: the worker is a
   per-turn interpreter whose completion queue nobody reads once its turn ends
   (agent/managed_worker.py), so the receipt obligation is the notice's only custody. The Desktop
   keeper leaves it while the worker lives and re-arms it once the worker is gone. Docstrings of
   `owes_tui_delivery` and `tui_gateway/completion_obligation.py` said workers never leave one; fixed.

2. Pause-kill duplicate (fixed). A core-update pause kills the chat's notify jobs with
   consume_output=False and journals each kill into the marker's killed_jobs, but the killed
   receipt kept its owner:"tui" obligation until the orderly exit journal settled it. Orderly exit:
   no duplicate (the exit journal settles it; test passes on base). Unclean death after the pause
   (SIGKILL/OOM, no exit journal): the next Desktop backend re-armed the obligation as a second
   notice beside the marker's report. `boundary_pause_hook` now settles the obligation of each job
   it actually killed (kill_state "killed") once the pause stands: custody transfer to the marker,
   as at backend exit. An `already_exited` job (marker has no real output) and a pause a user Stop
   beat keep their obligation.

Proof:
- tests/tui_gateway/test_tui_completion_obligation.py: 5 new tests (worker intent; pause ->
  orderly/unclean exit -> next backend; already_exited and user-Stop controls). RED on base:
  test_update_pause_kill_is_reported_once_from_the_marker[unclean] ("the killed job's notice was
  re-armed", armed=1); GREEN 18/18 with the fix.
- Mutants killed: dropping the kill_state filter (fails exited_before_kill); settling before the
  user-Stop check (fails user_stop_won); dropping the settle (fails unclean).
- 102 test files importing update_pause/completion_obligation/process_registry_obligations/
  exit_job_receipts: 1355 passed, 25 skipped. scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
